## Summary

| Vulnerability | Type | Severity | Function | Line(s) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Iterator Leak (defer after return) | High | `ProcessClaimsByRange` | 30-45 |
| 2 | Iterator Leak (conditional close) | High | `GetHighValueClaims` | 85-105 |
| 3 | Iterator Leak (manual close bypassed) | High | `ArchiveOldClaims` | 108-135 |

**Impact:** Each leaked iterator holds an open gRPC stream to the peer's state database. Under sustained load, this exhausts peer resources, causing denial of service. Fabric peers have limited iterator pools; leaks degrade performance and can crash the peer.

**Root Cause:** Inconsistent use of `defer` for resource cleanup. The code mixes `defer` (correct) with manual cleanup (error-prone) and places `defer` statements after early returns.
